@* The blocks of a page, tab or panel, one section gap (24px) apart (engineering/DESIGN.md > Layout > Spacing, #3095).
   Children carry no vertical margins of their own: any they bring are neutralised, so the gap is the design system's
   and never a page's. Follow a block with <SectionCaption> for helper text that describes it. *@
<div class="jim-section-stack @Class">
    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The blocks, top to bottom.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Classes for the stack itself, for horizontal or outer geometry only; never a vertical gap.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Class { get; set; }
}
